messages.content:
This is awesome — congratulations! I’d love to help make sure the message reaches the people who need it. A few quick questions so I can give the best recommendations and start drafting materials:

- What is the discovery and who stands to benefit (patients, clinicians, researchers, general public)?  
- Has the work been published or is there an embargo/press policy from a journal or funder?  
- When is the event (date/time) and what format are you planning (press conference, webinar, community town hall, hybrid)?  
- Any spokespeople confirmed (lead scientist, patient advocate, institutional leader)?  
- Constraints to watch for (privacy/consent, regulatory approvals, safety concerns, or messaging limitations)?

If you want, I can immediately:
- Draft a short, clear press release and a layperson-friendly summary;  
- Build a media/outreach list (journalists, patient groups, medical societies, policy contacts);  
- Create social posts and suggested visuals;  
- Produce an FAQ/Q&A to anticipate difficult questions and avoid overhyping;  
- Outline an event agenda with accessibility and live-streaming recommendations.

Pitfalls to avoid: overpromising results before peer review, ignoring accessibility/translation needs, and failing to provide clear next steps for people who want help or more info. Tell me the answers above or which draft you want first, and I’ll get started.
